      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of the parallelogram generated by two vectors $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$, we use the magnitude of their cross product: $\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}$. The area is then given by the absolute value of the determinant of the matrix formed by $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$.\n\nFirst, we need to compute $\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}$. The cross product is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} u_1 \\\\ u_2 \\\\ u_3 \\end{pmatrix} \\times \\begin{pmatrix} v_1 \\\\ v_2 \\\\ v_3 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} u_2v_3 - u_3v_2 \\\\ u_3v_1 - u_1v_3 \\\\ u_1v_2 - u_2v_1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nUsing the given vectors $\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}$, we can substitute into the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1\\cdot4 - (-2)\\cdot(-3) \\\\ -2\\cdot1 - 3\\cdot4 \\\\ 3\\cdot(-3) - 1\\cdot1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 - 6 \\\\ -2 - 12 \\\\ -9 - 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nNext, we find the magnitude of the resulting vector $\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}$:\n\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-14)^2 + (-10)^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 196 + 100} = \\sqrt{300} = 10\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{10\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]",
