      "text": "To find the area of the parallelogram generated by the vectors \\(\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we use the magnitude of their cross product.\n\nFirst, we need to calculate the cross product \\(\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\). The cross product of two vectors \\(\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} a_1 \\\\ a_2 \\\\ a_3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} b_1 \\\\ b_2 \\\\ b_3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{vmatrix}\n\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\\na_1 & a_2 & a_3 \\\\\nb_1 & b_2 & b_3\n\\end{vmatrix}\n\\]\n\nExpanding this determinant, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\\n3 & 1 & -2 \\\\\n1 & -3 & 4\n\\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nNow, we expand this determinant:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{i} \\left(1 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot (-3)\\right) - \\mathbf{j} \\left(3 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot 1\\right) + \\mathbf{k} \\left(3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1\\right)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\mathbf{i} (4 - 6) - \\mathbf{j} (12 + 2) + \\mathbf{k} (-9 - 1)\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= -2\\mathbf{i} - 14\\mathbf{j} - 10\\mathbf{k}\n\\]\n\nSo, $\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}$.\n\nNext, we need to find the magnitude of this vector to determine the area of the parallelogram:\n\n\\[\n\\left\\|\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\right\\| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-14)^2 + (-10)^2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\sqrt{4 + 196 + 100}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= \\sqrt{300}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= 10\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram is $10\\sqrt{3}$. Let's verify this with Python code.\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Vectors u and v\nu = np.array([3, 1, -2])\nv = np.array([1, -3, 4])\n\n# Calculate the cross product\ncross_product = np.cross(u, v)\n\n# Calculate the magnitude of the cross product\narea = np.sqrt(np.dot(cross_product, cross_product))\nprint(area)\n````\n17.320508075688775\n```\nThe calculated area of the parallelogram is approximately \\(17.32\\), which is equal to \\(10\\sqrt{3}\\). Thus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{10\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]",
