      "text": "To find the area of the parallelogram generated by the two vectors \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), we need to compute the magnitude of their cross product \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\).\n\nLet \\(\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\). The cross product \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\) is given by the determinant of the following matrix:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 4 \\end{vmatrix}\n\\]\n\nCalculating the determinant, we get:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{i} \\left(1 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot (-3)\\right) - \\mathbf{j} \\left(3 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot 1\\right) + \\mathbf{k} \\left(3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1\\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{i} (4 - 6) - \\mathbf{j} (12 + 2) + \\mathbf{k} (-9 - 1)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{i} (-2) - \\mathbf{j} (14) + \\mathbf{k} (-10)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe magnitude of this cross product is:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-14)^2 + (-10)^2}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\| = \\sqrt{4 + 196 + 100}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\| = \\sqrt{300}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\| = 10\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the parallelogram is \\(\\boxed{10\\sqrt{3}}\\).\n\nTo implement the solution in Python, we need to calculate the cross product, its magnitude, and then simplify the final expression. Let's do this using Python.\n```python\nimport numpy as np\r\n\r\n# Define the vectors\r\na = np.array([3, 1, -2])\r\nb = np.array([1, -3, 4])\r\n\r\n# Calculate the cross product\r\ncross_product = np.cross(a, b)\r\n\r\n# Calculate the magnitude of the cross product\r\nmagnitude = np.linalg.norm(cross_product)\r\nprint(magnitude)\n```",
